// test-error
// Issue #1159: a hex-sized array must be bounds-checked exactly like a
// decimal-sized one.
//
// TypeRegistrationEngine registered dimensions with Number.parseInt(text, 10),
// which reads "0x10" as 0 because parsing stops at 'x'. TypeValidator's
// checkArrayBounds guards with `dimensions[i] > 0`, so a mis-parsed 0 skipped
// validation entirely and the out-of-range write below was silently accepted.
// u8[16] and u8[0x10] declare the same array; only one of them was checked.
u8[0x10] data;

i32 main() {
    data[9999] <- 1;
    return 0;
}
